      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the table. it's a good start, but for a high-level coaching module, it feels a little too sanitized/positive. \n\nthe whole point of this simulation is to show how these perceptions can actually be *limiting* or even *damaging* to a career. for example, in the \"Emotional Intelligence\" row, calling the Maverick \"sensory/vivid/volatile\" sounds a bit poetic, but in a real boardroom, \"volatile\" is often used as a polite way to say they're emotionally unstable or lack self-control.\n\ncan you expand this into a detailed \"Perception Deep-Dive\" report? instead of just a table, i need a few paragraphs for each of those three categories (EQ, Decision-making, Crisis Response). \n\ni want you to write it from the perspective of a senior leadership consultant. for Candidate A, keep it as the \"idealized\" profile. but for Candidate B, i want you to lean into those more \"troubling\" interpretations. show how their linguistic style and \"unfiltered\" way of speaking causes peers to subconsciously categorize them as \"lacking nuance\" or \"prone to emotional outbursts,\" even if the data shows they are actually highly disciplined. \n\nwe need to show the trainees how much of a \"perception tax\" the Maverick has to pay just because they don't sound \"standard.\"",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
